[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1604","stub":{"id":"1604","section":"Rockingham to Clear Shade","altname":"","river":"Dark Shade Creek","difficulty":"IVtoV","states":["USA-PEN"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"3.14","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"levelFT","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"","id":"110332","location":{"latitude":"40.111239","longitude":"-78.808229"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":"","id":"115595","location":{"latitude":"40.148105","longitude":"-78.818418"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"2.82","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"101247378","title":null,"post_date":"2010-10-12 04:00:00+00","detail":"There is an undercut rock on River Left after the first significant drop. I walked and scouted the whole run at low water. At the drop there appears to be a left and right line. The left looks more fun but the main flow below the drop points directly to a large undercut rock. If the levels were 3 or 4 feet higher it would appear to be a solid rock. I will include a picture or two of the drop and then the rock.","user":{"name":"Michael Brant"}},{"id":"100661315","title":null,"post_date":"2008-12-19 05:00:00+00","detail":"About half way down the run, maybe a little further, a tree has fallen into the river in a fairly unattractive fashion. The tree is on the left side (cutbank) of the longest slide as the creek bends hard right. It looks to be obstructing the line a bit, but i could be wrong.","user":{"name":"Craig Leibfreid"}}],"photos":[{"id":"877304","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"877532","description":"This is the left Line, You can see the undercut rock.","caption":"Left Line","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/877304","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/877304"}},{"id":"877305","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"877533","description":"After some small steps there is a signficant drop which appears will have two lines at high water. The left line will have the main flow push you towards this undercut rock.","caption":"UnderCut Rock","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/877305","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/877305"}},{"id":"883645","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"886353","description":"This photo is just downstream of the \"undercut\" photo: https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/Photo/detail/photoid/877305/   \r\nBTW, at 6 inches on the river right gauge at the Wispering Pines bridge, the undercut is easy to avoid, even when passing in front of it.","caption":"Carolyn at ledge","poi_name":"","subject":"Carolyn DeVenney","author":"Jeff Macklin","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/883645","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/883645"}}],"detail":{"id":"1604","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"See the [Benscreek Canoe Club Stonycreek Watershed Page](https://benscreekcanoeclub.com/river-talk/rivers/).\n\nFor other streams in this watershed, check out:\n\n[Stony Canyon](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/2843/) (III-IV)\n\n[Stony Gorge](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/2847/) (IV)\n\n[Roaring Fork](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/2829/) (IV)\n\n[Shade Creek](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/1659/) (III-IV)\n\n[Paint Creek](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/2844/) (V)\n\n[Clear Shade Creek](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/1593/) (III)\n\n[Conemaugh River](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/1596/